2606.13178,2606.13178,"5,6",cross_page,"According to the definitions and propositions in the text, if a frozen representation H⋆₁ is Bayes-minimal for a source loss ℓ₁ and ℓ₁ is strictly refined by a target loss ℓ₂ (i.e., ℓ₁ ≺P ℓ₂), what can be said about the frozen-transfer excess risk E_{ℓ₂,P}(H⋆₁) when the target Bayes risk is finite?","E_{ℓ₂,P}(H⋆₁) is strictly positive and finite whenever R⋆_{ℓ₂,P}(H⋆₁) < ∞.","Definition 4 (Strict loss refinement). The notation ℓ1 ≺P ℓ2 means that ℓ1 ⪯P ℓ2 and σ(qℓ2,P (X)) ̸⊆σ(qℓ1,P (X)) mod PX.","Consequently, when the target Bayes risk is finite, Eℓ2,P (H⋆ 1) = R⋆ ℓ2,P (H⋆ 1) −R⋆ ℓ2,P ∈(0, ∞], with finite positive excess whenever R⋆ ℓ2,P (H⋆ 1) < ∞.","PAGE A defines strict loss refinement (ℓ₁ ≺P ℓ₂), while PAGE B states the consequence for the frozen-transfer excess risk under this condition.",reject,multihop-v1,0.000,0.600,"single_page_sufficient(page_B,f1=0.60)"
2606.13178,2606.13178,"6,7",cross_page,"According to the paper, what is the exact expression for the excess log-loss risk Elog,P(H⋆_1) when H⋆_1 is Bayes-minimal for a loss ℓ1 such that ℓ1 ≺P ℓlog?","Elog,P(H⋆_1) = E[DKL(P(Y | X) ∥ P(Y | H⋆_1))] > 0.","Proposition 3.2 (Qualitative loss-shift obstruction). Let ℓ1 and ℓ2 be losses that admit Bayes quotients under P. Assume ℓ1 ≺P ℓ2. If H⋆ 1 = h⋆ 1(X) is Bayes-minimal for (P, ℓ1), then H⋆ 1 is not Bayes-sufficient for (P, ℓ2). ... Consequently, when the target Bayes risk is finite, Eℓ2,P (H⋆ 1) = R⋆ ℓ2,P (H⋆ 1) −R⋆ ℓ2,P ∈(0, ∞], with finite positive excess whenever R⋆ ℓ2,P (H⋆ 1) < ∞.","Combining Theorem 3.3 with Proposition 3.2, suppose that ℓ1 is a pretraining loss admitting a Bayes quotient under P and that ℓ1 ≺P ℓlog. If H⋆ 1 = h⋆ 1(X) is Bayes-minimal for (P, ℓ1), then Elog,P (H⋆ 1) = E [ DKL ( P(Y | X) ∥P(Y | H⋆ 1) ) ] > 0.","PAGE A defines the loss-shift obstruction and the concept of Bayes-minimal representations for ℓ1 ≺P ℓ2, while PAGE B gives the exact quantitative expression for the excess log-loss risk in this case.",reject,multihop-v1,0.000,0.800,"single_page_sufficient(page_B,f1=0.80)"
