2606.13178,2606.13178,"9,10",cross_page,"What is the exact population conditional-KL gap (in nats) for the Bayes-class representation S in the main m = 5 setting, and what does this gap quantify in terms of loss shift between representations?",0.058506 nats; it quantifies the excess log risk (NLL gap) incurred by S relative to the full representation X due to loss of probability-relevant information.,"For the main m = 5 setting, this population conditional-KL gap is 0.058506 nats for Hcls = S.","NLL and the conditional-KL gap are the primary measures of loss shift in this experiment. The Bayes-class representation can be calibrated relative to its coarsened information, because its optimal forecast is E[η(X) | S]. It is strictly less informative and strictly worse under proper scoring rules. The central empirical effect is a loss of probability-relevant information, measured exactly by NLL and the conditional-KL gap.","PAGE A provides the exact value of the conditional-KL gap for S, while PAGE B explains that this gap measures the loss of probability-relevant information and is the primary measure of loss shift.",pending,multihop-v1,0.507,0.364,needs_both_pages
2606.13178,2606.13178,"10,11",cross_page,"According to the controlled binary model, what is the excess negative log likelihood (NLL) of the Bayes-class representation S relative to the full representation X, and why does this excess occur despite both representations achieving the same classification accuracy?","0.058389 ± 0.000161; because S discards probability information relevant for log loss, even though it is classification-optimal.","The representation S is classification-optimal and strictly suboptimal for log loss because it collapses inputs with different conditional probabilities. The partially coars- ened representation lies between the full and Bayes-class representations, consistent with retaining part of the log- loss-relevant information.","Bayes class S
0.058389 ± 0.000161",PAGE A explains why S is suboptimal for log loss despite being classification-optimal; PAGE B gives the quantitative excess NLL value for S relative to X.,pending,multihop-v1,0.269,0.333,needs_both_pages
