2606.13285,2606.13285,"2,3",cross_page,"According to the definitions and constraints provided, what is the sum of the proportions γi for all systems in the ensemble M S, and what equation expresses this constraint?","The sum of the proportions γi for all systems in the ensemble M S is always 1, as expressed in Eq. 2: ∑_{i=1}^n γi = 1, n ≥ 2.","Definition 1: An ensemble of multiple systems M S consists of n systems, denoted as the set S = (s1, . . . , sn) ∈Rn, where n ∈N+; n ≥2, and each si is a distinct system. This definition shows our approach require two or more systems. For simplicity of notation, we use si to denote the target variable of System si. For example, in the context of epidemic forecasting, si represents the number of daily new cases in system si, or region i. Similarly, we use M S to denote the ensemble of multiple systems, as well as the aggregate of the target variables across all systems. That is, M S = Pn i=1 si , n ≥2.","n X i=1 γi = 1, n ≥2. (2)","PAGE A defines the ensemble M S and the meaning of γi as the proportion of each system, while PAGE B provides the explicit constraint equation that their sum is always 1.",reject,multihop-v1,0.791,0.939,"single_page_sufficient(page_B,f1=0.94)"
