2606.13380,2606.13380,"13,14",cross_page,"What is the observed effect of the 'Exploration' component on the stability and quality of initial candidates in the quantum feature map task, and how is this effect visually represented in the ablation study results?","The 'Exploration' component improves both the quality and stability of initial candidates in the quantum feature map task, as shown by higher mean accuracy and reduced variance in the upper left panel of Fig. 6.","As shown in the upper panel of Fig. 6, the “Exploration” component improves the qual- ity and stability of initial candidates. In the quantum feature map task, the Trial 1 accuracy increases from 0.8567 ± 0.0626 without Exploration to 0.9562 ± 0.0026 with the default setting, indicating higher performance together with a substantial reduction in variance.",FIG. 6: Results of the ablation study for the quantum feature map and VQE ansatz generation tasks. Solid lines show the mean of the best performance across five independent runs for each trial. Shaded bands denote the standard error of the mean. The two graphs in the upper panel compare the system with the version without the “Exploration” component.,"PAGE A provides the quantitative effect of the 'Exploration' component on accuracy and variance, while PAGE B describes how these effects are visualized in the upper panel of Fig. 6.",reject,multihop-v1,0.915,0.000,"single_page_sufficient(page_A,f1=0.92)"
