2606.13380,2606.13380,"19,20",cross_page,"According to the agent system's experimental setup, what is the required argument and its type for specifying the qubits when constructing a qml.CNOT operation within the quantum circuit search process that uses 10 qubits?",The required argument is 'wires' of type 'Sequence[int]'.,The circuit templates for both the quantum feature map for QML and ansatz for VQE are independent of the number of qubits. The qubit counts reported here correspond to the configurations evaluated during the quantum circuit search process performed by the proposed agentic framework.,"""args"": [ { ""name"": ""wires"", ""type"": ""Sequence[int]"", ""required"": true, ""description"": ""A sequence of two integers specifying the wires (qubits) that the CNOT gate acts on. The first wire in the sequence is the control qubit, and the second is the target qubit. For example, [0, 1] applies the CNOT with control on wire 0 and target on wire 1."" },","PAGE A provides the context that the quantum circuit search process uses specific qubit counts (e.g., 10 qubits), while PAGE B defines the required argument ('wires' of type 'Sequence[int]') for constructing a qml.CNOT operation.",pending,multihop-v1,0.000,0.429,needs_both_pages
2606.13380,2606.13380,"20,21",cross_page,"After preprocessing the MNIST images for the quantum feature map experiment, how many principal components are used as input features, and on which subset of the MNIST data is the quantum feature map generation process performed?","80 principal components are used as input features, and the quantum feature map generation process is performed on the MNIST training dataset.","The MNIST dataset consists of 70,000 handwritten digit images, each of which is a 28×28 grayscale image labeled with one of the digits from 0 to 9. MNIST is officially divided into 60,000 training images and 10,000 test images. Our agentic system uses a sampled subset of the training data and do not use any of the test set. When it finishes the iterative improvements of the feature maps, we evaluate the feature maps generated from the system on the entire test dataset.","In this work, we use the top 80 principal components as input features and normalize the data to the range [0, 1]. This preprocessing procedure is fixed throughout all experiments. The agentic system does not observe the original image data at any stage and is not allowed to modify the preprocessing pipeline.","PAGE A provides the information about using the MNIST training data for the quantum feature map generation process, while PAGE B specifies that 80 principal components are used as input features after preprocessing.",reject,multihop-v1,0.000,1.000,"single_page_sufficient(page_B,f1=1.00)"
