2606.13380,2606.13380,"24,25",cross_page,"Which of the benchmark ansatzes described has a parameter count that scales as O(kN^2), and what is the main structural feature that allows its circuit depth to remain substantially lower than UCCSD?","The k-UpCCSD ansatz has a parameter count that scales as O(kN^2), and its main structural feature is the use of sparse, pair-preserving double excitations repeated in k layers, which keeps the circuit depth substantially lower than UCCSD.","3. k-UpCCSD ansatz [18]: The k-UpCCSD ansatz is a sparse unitary coupled cluster construction based on the observation that a significant fraction of electron correlation can be captured by generalized single excitations together with pair-preserving double excitations. A single UpCCSD layer applies these excitations once, and the ansatz increases expressivity systematically by repeating the layer k times. Here T ℓ
