2606.13380,2606.13380,"26,27",cross_page,"According to the analysis of the agentic system's performance, what was the lowest cost function value achieved in the best experiment for the ansatz generation task for VQE, and what component is plausibly attributed to enabling critical assessment of generated ideas during iterative refinement?","The lowest cost function value achieved was below 5 × 10−2, and the 'Discussion' component is plausibly attributed to enabling critical assessment of generated ideas.","Furthermore, we summarize the seed ideas that led to the best-performing quantum feature map and ansatz for VQE, providing insight into the initial hypotheses explored by the system. Additional investigations are conducted on the properties of the generated feature maps through kernel matrix analysis. Finally, we analyze the impact of optional circuit modules included in the best-performing ansatz, focusing on the relationship between parameter count, gate count, and estimation accuracy.","Nevertheless, all experiments exhibited multiple instances of improvement across successive trials, ultimately reducing the cost function to below 5 × 10−2. Notably, the experiment shown in red, which produced the best final solution, had the second highest cost function value in its first trial among all five experiments. This suggests that the relationship between the quality of the initial idea and the final outcome is not straightforward. This behavior suggests that a detailed examination of the refinement process is required, but it is plausibly attributed to the newly introduced “Discussion” component, which enables critical and even negative assessment of generated ideas during iterative refinement.","PAGE A provides context that the analysis concerns the best-performing ansatz for VQE, while PAGE B gives the specific lowest cost value achieved and attributes the improvement to the 'Discussion' component.",reject,multihop-v1,0.000,0.721,"single_page_sufficient(page_B,f1=0.