2606.13629,2606.13629,"6,7",cross_page,"According to Theorem 1, what is the lower bound on the coverage probability for the confidence interval CI output by Algorithm 1, and what is the reasoning that justifies this bound?","The lower bound is 1 − (α1 + α2 + α3), justified by combining the probabilities that the synthetic-data target and the real–synthetic gap are covered, using a union bound.","Theorem 1. Suppose Assumptions 1 and 2 hold. Then, the confidence interval CI output by Algorithm 1 satisfies P (θ∗∈CI) ≥1 −(α1 + α2 + α3).","Therefore, combining equations (1) and (4) yields P (θ∗∈CI) ≥P  ˜θ ∈[˜L, ˜U], ∆T +1 ∈[ ˆ∆L, ˆ∆U]  ≥1 −(α1 + α2 + α3).","PAGE A provides the formal statement of the coverage bound in Theorem 1, while PAGE B explains the reasoning and probability combination that justifies this bound.",pending,multihop-v1,0.444,0.444,needs_both_pages
