2606.13629,2606.13629,"8,9",cross_page,"According to the weighted inference procedure for non-exchangeable tasks, what is the formula for the normalized weight assigned to the current task, and how is this weight used in the computation of the weighted quantiles for the confidence interval endpoints?","The normalized weight for the current task is \( \bar{w}_{T+1} = \frac{1}{1 + \sum_{j=1}^T w_j} \), and it is used as the coefficient of the atom at \(-\infty\) (for the lower endpoint) or \(+\infty\) (for the upper endpoint) in the weighted quantile computation for the confidence interval endpoints.","Let w1,...,wT ∈[0,1] be fixed weights assigned to the historical tasks, and define normalized weights ¯wi = wi 1 + PT j=1 wj , i ∈[T ], ¯wT +1 = 1 1 + PT j=1 wj . The condition wi ≤1 ensures ¯wi ≤¯wT +1, so the current task receives at least as much weight as any indi- vidual historical task. We consider setting ˆ∆L and ˆ∆U as weighted quantiles of the historical gaps. For a probability distribution ν on the real line, let Qγ(ν) denote its γ-quantile.1 We define the weighted endpoints at error level γ as ˆ∆L = Qγ   T X j=1 ¯wjδ ˆ∆L j + ¯wT +1δ−∞  , ˆ∆U = Q1−γ   T X j=1 ¯wjδ ˆ∆U j + ¯wT +1δ+∞  .","5: Define normalized weights ¯wi = wi 1+PT j=1 wj for i ∈[T ], and ¯wT +1 = 1 1+PT j=1 wj 6: Let ˆ∆L = Q α3 2 12PT j=1 ¯wjδ ˆ∆L j + ¯wT +1δ−∞ 13 and ˆ∆U = Q1−α3 2 12PT j=1 ¯wjδ ˆ∆U j + ¯wT +1δ+∞ 13 Output: Confidence interval for θ∗: CI = [˜L + ˆ∆L, ˜U + ˆ∆U]","PAGE A defines the normalized weights including the current task and explains their role in the weighted quantile, while PAGE B gives the explicit formula for the current task's normalized weight and shows its use in the quantile computation in Algorithm 2.",reject,multihop-v1,0.880,0.692,"single_page_sufficient(page_A,f1=0.88)"
2606.13629,2606.13629,"9,10",cross_page,"In the multi-dimensional extension, what is the form of the confidence region for θ∗ output by Algorithm 3 when the nested convex family is chosen as Dr = c + rB, and how is Rj computed in this case?","The confidence region is CI = fCI ⊕ (c + ˆR B), where Rj = sup_{δ∈Kj} γB(δ − c) and γB(x) = inf{r : x ∈ rB}.","Let {Dr : r ∈R} be a fixed family of subsets of Rd satisfying the following conditions: for each finite r, Dr is convex and compact; if r ≤r′, then Dr ⊆Dr′; S r∈R Dr = Rd; and for every compact set K ⊆Rd, the value R(K) := inf{r : K ⊆Dr} satisfies K ⊆DR(K). The last condition is a mild right-continuity condition on the family. We also use the convention D+∞= Rd. For a point δ ∈Rd, the associated scalar score is ρ(δ) = inf{r : δ ∈Dr}.","The choice of nested family determines the shape of the resulting confidence region. A useful default is a translated and scaled convex family. Let B ⊆Rd be a convex compact set containing the origin in its interior, and define Dr = c + rB, r ≥0, with Dr = ∅for r < 0. If γB(x) = inf{r : x ∈rB}, then Rj = sup δ∈Kj γB(δ −c). The set B can be the Euclidean unit ball, or a d-dimensional rectangle, for example.","PAGE A defines the general nested convex family {Dr} and the scalar score ρ(δ), while PAGE B specifies the form Dr = c + rB and how to compute Rj and the resulting confidence region.",reject,multihop-v1,0.246,0.789,"single_page_sufficient(page_B,f1=0.79)"
2606.13629,2606.13629,"10,11",cross_page,"According to the procedures described, what is the coverage guarantee for the confidence interval output by Algorithm 4 for the finite-sample target θ∗(S), and how does this compare to the coverage guarantee for the confidence region output by Algorithm 3 for the population target θ∗?","Algorithm 4 guarantees P(θ∗(S) ∈ CI) ≥ 1 − α, while Algorithm 3 guarantees P(θ∗ ∈ CI) ≥ 1 − (α1 + α2 + α3).","Theorem 3. Suppose Assumptions 1 and 2 hold. Then, the confidence region CI output by Algorithm 3 satisfies P (θ∗∈CI) ≥1 −(α1 + α2 + α3).","Theorem 4. Suppose Assumption 1 holds. Then, the confidence interval CI output by Algorithm 4 satisfies P (θ∗(S) ∈CI) ≥1 −α.","PAGE A gives the coverage guarantee for Algorithm 3 (population target), while PAGE B gives the coverage guarantee for Algorithm 4 (finite-sample target).",pending,multihop-v1,0.000,0.000,needs_both_pages
